// @vibe/compiler (top level) — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract.
// This is the FINAL directory in the whole #897 vpkg-migration series: every
// other directory in the repo (all lib/@vibe/*, lib/@vibex/*, and all ten
// subdirectories of lib/@vibe/compiler/ itself) already has an index.vpkg.
// The old plain index.vibe was NOT a pure facade — it was (and, renamed, is)
// a substantial real implementation file (selfbuild_entry, the
// selfbuild_probe_*/selfbuild_stage1_probe_* families, build_cli_adapter_bytes,
// ...), so per the established rename convention (`git mv index.vibe
// <dirname>.vibe`; see checker/checker_facade.vibe's note for why a
// collision sometimes forces a different name) it became `compiler.vibe`
// (no collision here — verified before the move).
//
// version annotation fix: the old `export let version = "0.0.1"` had no type
// annotation, which check_contract rejects for a non-fn top-level let (#752
// requires `let name: Type` bodyless contract decls to match a "val <type>"
// implementation fingerprint, which in turn requires the implementation's
// own let to be annotated) — changed to `export let version: String =
// "0.0.1"` (same fix pattern as core/core.vibe earlier in this series).
// The same annotation gap existed on 12 more `export let compiler_X = Y`
// plain-alias bindings in compiler.vibe (re-exporting syntax/parser
// functions under `compiler_`-prefixed names) and one in
// coverage_suite_run.vibe (`parse_line_list_export`) — all now annotated
// with the aliased function's real type so they satisfy the same "val
// <type>" fingerprint as bodyless `let name: Type` contract lines below.
//
// Directory-shared-scope package (44 impl files + this contract). Several
// hazard categories turned up, each resolved the same way prior #897
// batches resolved their analogous case:
//
// (1) `_cli_adapter_module_source.vibe` (formerly cli_adapter_module_source.vibe):
// an auto-generated (scripts/generate_bundle.sh), fully self-contained
// flattened snapshot of the ENTIRE compiler — ~789 top-level exports,
// including its own from-scratch `enum Pat`/`Expr`/`Stmt`/`TypeExpr`/`Type`/
// `TypeDef`/`TypeEnv`/`Subst` (mangled `_exp_lib__<path>`-suffixed
// bindings for everything else). It is read only as literal source text by
// coverage/RC-verification scripts (never `import`ed by any .vibe file), so
// declaring ~789 bodyless signatures here would be both impractical and
// pointless. Excluded via the leading-underscore exemption
// (contract_sibling_impl_raws, loader/header_cache.vibe:355) — the same
// mechanism used below for every other file in this list. ~15 script/doc
// references updated to the new name in a prior commit on this branch;
// scripts/generations.sh + generations_test.sh (an unrelated build-output
// artifact in a scratch `out_dir` that only coincidentally shares the old
// basename) and docs/archive/moonbit-retirement.md (historical record) were
// deliberately left alone.
//
// (2) Standalone alternate-entry-point files: several top-level files are
// individually fs-compiled programs (their own `main`/`cli_main`/
// `compile_cli_request`/`selfbuild_entry`/`selfbuild_compile_stage2`/
// `selfbuild_probe_type_db_*` are never part of the old facade's public
// surface), so declaring their names here would either (a) be pure
// contract pollution for genuinely dead/orphaned code, or (b) in the cases
// that share a name with a real canonical implementation, risk the
// facade's first-impl-unit-wins allocation silently swapping in a stub.
// Verified via zero manifest/script references (or, for the cli_main/main/
// compile_cli_request-sharing files, the ABSENCE of any reference besides
// each other) before excluding: _cli_core_entry.vibe, _cli_command_entry.vibe,
// _cli_component_entry.vibe, _cli_gc_entry.vibe (all orphaned variants
// colliding with cli_adapter.vibe's real `cli_main` or with each other),
// _cli.vibe, _cli_stage1_entry.vibe, _bench_file_compile_mode_same_content_run.vibe,
// _bench_loader_manifest_groups_run.vibe, _bench_loader_manifest_list_run.vibe,
// _cst_lower_coverage_run.vibe (orphaned standalone bench/coverage drivers,
// several sharing a private `main`), _selfbuild_runtime_entry.vibe (the
// hand-source later embedded as a string into selfbuild_runtime_entry_bundle.vibe;
// its own `export fn selfbuild_entry()` is a trivial stub, not compiler.vibe's
// real one), _slim_entry.vibe (an alternate `selfbuild_compile_stage2`
// entry using a leaner import set), _selfbuild_gate_block_a.vibe (a
// standalone gate-testing "block" that duplicates cache_probe_support.vibe's
// entire selfbuild_probe_type_db_* family plus string_to_bytes/
// remove_file_if_exists, reached only via its own dedicated test's direct
// leaf import). scripts/generate_bundle.sh, compiler_sources_manifest.tsv,
// and the dependent test files' import paths were updated accordingly in a
// prior commit on this branch.
//
// (3) Test-only fixture files reached exclusively via a direct leaf import
// from their own dedicated tests/*_test.vibe (never through this package's
// facade): _import_alias_collision_a/b.vibe, _import_private_ctor_collision_a/b.vibe,
// _import_private_type_collision_a/b.vibe (each pair's colliding `answer`/
// `Same`/`Token` names are exactly what their tests exist to prove don't
// collide when imported via alias — the whole point breaks if they were
// merged into one shared scope), and _import_alias_codegen_support.vibe
// (a lone `answer` fixture for a similar aliased-import test). Excluded the
// same way, with the 5 dependent tests' import paths updated.
//
// (4) _codegen_common.vibe: a large (~150-name) plain-import + bare
// `export { ... }` re-export file with ZERO consumers anywhere in the repo
// (not even a test) — codegen_gc.vibe, its sibling with the same shape, IS
// consumed by tests/inline_wasm_test.vibe via direct leaf import, so it
// stays a normal (zero-declaration) member below. Note on the bare-export
// form: `export { name }` (no `./file` prefix) parses as SExport, which
// neither collect_impl_fn_defs/collect_impl_type_defs (only see direct
// SLet/SStruct/... defs) nor collect_reexported_names (only sees
// SReExport, i.e. `export ./file { name }`) ever inspects — such names are
// invisible to check_contract and MUST NOT be declared here (declaring one
// produces "has no implementation", since no direct def or SReExport
// backs it). This is why compiler.vibe's own trailing bare `export { ... }`
// block (a leftover from the plain-index.vibe era) is only a partial guide
// to this contract's real surface — names it lists that compiler.vibe only
// ever plain-`import`ed from entry/cli_cache, entry/compiler/fs_compile, or
// entry/source_compile (compile_source, compile_source_wasi,
// compile_with_modules*, compile_file_fs*, parse_batch_jobs_tsv,
// prepare_jobs_cached, compile_jobs_cached, selfbuild_probe_cli_cache_counts,
// selfbuild_probe_cli_file_cache_counts) are NOT declared below for the same
// reason; they simply are not part of this package's new external surface
// (a real, accepted behavior change from the plain-index.vibe era, same
// class of change as checker_facade.vibe's superseded hand-written list).
// selfbuild_probe_type_db_* names ARE declared below despite also being
// plain-imported by compiler.vibe, because cache_probe_support.vibe (a
// normal member of this package) exports them directly with a real SLet def.
//
// (5) cli_probe_entry.vibe -> _cli_probe_entry.vibe: an orphaned standalone
// arg/compile-probe harness (probe_arg0_len/probe_compile_len/...), zero
// consumers anywhere in the repo (same shape as the (2) group above), so it
// would ordinarily just join that list. It gets its own note because
// excluding it isn't optional the way the (2)/(4) exclusions are: this file
// imports `read_arg` from `../cli/dispatch.vibe`, and dispatch.vibe (the
// `lib/@vibe/cli` package's entry point) in turn depends on this compiler
// package. Every other #897 batch was a one-directional "downward" edge (the
// compiler importing an already-migrated leaf package), so the new
// directory-wide index.vpkg never had to represent a dependency back onto
// itself. `lib/@vibe/cli` -> `lib/@vibe/compiler` is exactly that reverse
// edge, and it is real (the CLI genuinely needs the compiler) -- it simply
// never round-tripped through a single shared-scope node before. With this
// file's `{}` presence-only import counted as a normal package dependency
// edge (ADR-0070 Phase 1's ".vpkg gets implicit membership unconditionally"
// merges auto-discovered siblings with explicit ones -- header_cache.vibe's
// contract_sibling_impl_raws/merge_impl_raws_dedupe -- so leaving the import
// out without renaming would not have helped: auto-discovery re-adds any
// non-underscore .vibe file in the directory), `index.vpkg`'s own dependency
// list included this file, which depends on dispatch.vibe, which resolves
// its own `import ../compiler { ... }` back to this SAME index.vpkg node --
// a same-node self-loop the type_db fs-mode cycle detector
// (runtime/typecheck_fs.vibe::ensure_fingerprint_fs_go) rightly rejects.
// Confirmed against a rebuilt (not stale-cached) stage1 compiler with a
// minimal external `import ../compiler { lex, parse_program }` repro: the
// live cycle stack was exactly
// repro -> index.vpkg -> cli_probe_entry.vibe -> cli/dispatch.vibe -> index.vpkg.
// Renamed with the leading-underscore exemption (same mechanism as the (2)
// group) so contract_sibling_impl_raws' auto-discovery skips it entirely,
// removing the edge instead of papering over one instance of it.
//
// (6) coverage_suite_run.vibe -> _coverage_suite_run.vibe: fixing (5) let
// db_typecheck_fs's fs-mode graph walk proceed past the cycle for the first
// time for ANY external consumer of this package, and it immediately hit a
// second, independent, pre-existing problem living in this file specifically
// -- confirmed unrelated to (5) by reproducing it standalone (`vibe test
// lib/@vibe/compiler/coverage_suite_run.vibe` fails identically with zero
// involvement of cli_probe_entry.vibe or index.vpkg). Two layered issues,
// both now fixed here:
//   (a) its `test { }` block called `Double::parse`, which is declared in
//   builtins_extended.vibe's lookup_numeric (dead scaffolding -- referenced
//   only by that file's own dedicated test, never wired into the real
//   checker) but is NOT an actual checker-known builtin (#776; see
//   lib/@vibex/wasm/wat_encoder/wat_encoder.vibe's parse_decimal_double,
//   which hand-rolls the identical workaround for the identical reason).
//   Replaced the three call sites with a small local decimal parser
//   (parse_rate_double) instead of adding real Double::parse support
//   (out of scope for this batch) or reaching into wat_encoder's fuller,
//   scientific-notation-capable version across an unrelated package.
//   (b) even once it compiles, the test block itself is unconditional: it
//   `assert(false)`s unless VIBE_SUITE_REPORT_LIST/JSON/SUMMARY env vars are
//   set. `vibe test`'s `_start` runs every test block in the WHOLE merged
//   program, not just the entry file's own -- so as soon as this file's
//   `test{}` genuinely entered any external consumer's compiled graph (via
//   this package's blanket re-export), that consumer's own test run started
//   failing on an unrelated, unconfigured "coverage suite run" test it never
//   asked for. Confirmed exactly the same failure independent of import
//   depth (lib/@vibe/cli/dispatch_test.vibe and 4 others, all through
//   dispatch.vibe -> this package). This mirrors (5)'s hazard exactly:
//   `coverage_suite_run.vibe` is itself an unreferenced standalone driver
//   (zero consumers of parse_line_list_export anywhere in the repo, same
//   verification as (2)/(5); not invoked by scripts/coverage_suite.sh or any
//   Taskfile/pkspec target under its own name either -- fully dead as an
//   entry point today), so it gets the same leading-underscore exclusion.
// Kept the Double::parse fix even though the file is now excluded from the
// package's facade: it is a real, independently-confirmed bug (not just a
// vpkg-migration side effect), so leaving the file compilable on its own
// (e.g. a future direct `vibe test` invocation) costs nothing and is simply
// correct.
//
// Bodyless-declaration conventions used below (matching prior batches):
// `fn` for every real function (whether written as `export fn` or
// `export let name = (...) -> T { ... }`, an EFn-valued let — checker/checker.vibe,
// core/index.vpkg's builtin_registry.vibe entries, etc. established
// this precedent); `let name: Type` (no `opaque`) for a real VALUE let,
// fingerprinted as "val <type>" (version, the compiler_* aliases,
// parse_line_list_export, the *_path/*_source string constants in
// selfbuild_gate_sources_{a,b,c}.vibe); bodyless `type Name` (no `opaque`
// keyword — parse_contract_program treats bare `type Name` exactly like
// `opaque type Name` for conformance, "opacity is only a documentation-level
// difference", contract/contract.vibe:131-134) for every package-owned
// struct/enum whose real definition lives in its impl file
// (AstBinaryReader, CheckError, NodeKind, CstChild, the 6 coverage_suite_lib
// structs); Expr/Pat/Stmt/TypeExpr/Type/TypeDef/TypeEnv/Subst/Token/TypeDb
// are cross-package re-exports (from core/, syntax/, runtime/) and are
// likewise declared bodyless per those packages' own established
// convention (core/index.vpkg, syntax/index.vpkg, runtime/index.vpkg).

